{"DualWriterMode3 records legacy-duration metrics when Storage.Create fails (and similarly for Storage.Update), corrupting legacy vs storage latency/error dashboards by misattributing storage failures to the legacy histogram and using the storage timing window": 0.9809916615486145, "DualWriterMode3.DeleteCollection records the legacy DeleteCollection duration into the storage-duration metric, corrupting storage latency/error metrics and making storage dashboards/alerts unreliable for delete-collection operations": 0.980732262134552, "Mode3 is not selectable from config - even when DualWriterDesiredModes is configured to Mode3, SetDualWritingMode defaults an unset key to Mode1 and provides no transition into Mode3, so fresh deployments won't actually run Mode3 and integration tests won't validate Mode3 behavior on a clean KV store": 0.31907621026039124, "TestMode3_Create configures only Legacy.Create for the failing case, but DualWriterMode3.Create calls Storage.Create first, causing the storage mock to receive an unexpected call and fail before the intended assertion, making the Mode3 unit test suite unstable/incorrect": 0.9270272850990295}